The app is built in `src/` (App.tsx plus desk.ts, IssuesPage.tsx, IssueDetail.tsx, HelpPage.tsx and SettingsPage.tsx) and passes `./check` and all 30 visible tests, using 4 of the 15 runs. It uses @tanstack/react-query for loading and optimistic updates, with rollback on refusal. I was unsure about the decline paths, which the visible tests don't cover: the assign error reads `assign error: declined`, since the brief gave no prefix; related help is searched by the title as it was when the detail first loaded; and the settings name is trimmed only for the required check, not the saved value. The console 404 is probably the favicon.